<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Lisbon</h1><p class="st-meta">1022 CE – 1034 CE (approx.) · capital Lisbon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A brief taifa at Lisbon on the Tagus estuary, held by the heirs of the freedman Sabur before its absorption by Badajoz.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> had been part of the territory controlled by the freedman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabur-al-saqlabi">Sabur al-Saqlabi</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a>. When he died in 1022 and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> seized Badajoz, Sabur's sons are said to have kept Lisbon as a separate principality.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from a few lines in Arabic chronicles, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> consisted of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> and its estuary, an Atlantic port trading in fish, salt and agricultural produce. Its rulers had no lasting dynasty or court to speak of.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By 1034 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aftasid-dynasty">Aftasids</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-badajoz">Taifa of Badajoz</a> had absorbed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>. It stayed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> until 1093, was briefly ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a>, then passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-kongo">Afonso I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a> took it in 1147 with the help of crusaders.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1022 CE – 1034 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:80.04%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1022 CE – 1034 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lisbon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd al-Aziz ibn Sabur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Mozarabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Lisbon</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1028&amp;focus=taifa-of-lisbon" aria-label="Taifa of Lisbon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4453 789 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Lisbon lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4773 1045L4827 1039"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4827 1039h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4773 1045h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lisbon. <a href="/atlas?year=1028&amp;focus=taifa-of-lisbon">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
